      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Inconsistent color transfer often points to issues with the sublimation paper or the pigment itself. Ensure your sublimation ink is fresh and that the transfer paper is not damaged or expired, as these materials degrade quickly. Also, check the fabric pretreatment process; if the polyester fabric isn't properly pretreated, the dye won't bond correctly, leading to washed-out results.",
