    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We checked the ink and the paper and they both seem fine. All the batches use the same materials. It's weird because the machine settings are identical every time, but we just get these random gaps in pigment. It's almost like the ink is just... disappearing mid-process. Is there any way environmental factors like humidity or even subtle shifts in how the paper is laid down could cause the dye to just fail to show up?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
