    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, we'll look into the humidity and the plate temperature. But the pattern is what's really bothering me. It's not just a general fade; sometimes it looks like specific little sections of the design just get eaten away or ignored by the heat, almost like something is interfering with the ink right at the moment of transfer. Is there any chemical or technical reason why the pigment would fail in such a localized, irregular way?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
