      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Localized pigment failure strongly suggests an issue with thermal contact or transfer material integrity in those specific spots. Look closely for tiny debris, dust, or residue on the hot plate that could be creating micro-cold spots, interrupting the required heat transfer. Alternatively, if the design has very thin lines, there might be a localized saturation issue where the ink load is too sparse for consistent transfer.",
